## Summary

- Bind Python unittest imports only when static syntax proves the imported module is the declared deliverable.
- Treat `from package import name` as ambiguous because Python may resolve the name as either a submodule or package attribute.
- Count only unconditional module-level imports; conditional and function-local imports do not establish binding.
- Add regressions for ambiguous package attributes, conditional imports, and function-local imports while retaining explicit module-qualified import coverage.

## Validation

- CLI build passed in an isolated HOME/XDG environment.
